WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:10.346
That evening Ally, Mateo, Bethany, Kate, and Julius gathered at Ray's house to start writing letters to the mayor.

2
00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:14.605
"It was nice of your dad to let us come here to write letters," Julius said.

3
00:00:14.606 --> 00:00:18.014
"He loves having people over," Mateo said.

4
00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:22.896
"He said he and Flo will write letters later, after they get back from seeing a movie.

5
00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:26.005
And he'll buy five T-shirts too!"

6
00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:28.596
"Woo-hoo!" Ally said.

7
00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:34.425
"I've texted everyone I know, asking them to text everyone they know to write letters," Kate said.

8
00:00:34.426 --> 00:00:37.368
"I told them we're making a petition too."

9
00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:41.564
"What do you think of this?" Bethany held up a banner she was making:

10
00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:45.364
"Soccer Fields Are More Important than Parking Lots!"

11
00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:49.030
"That's so great!" Mateo gushed.

12
00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:55.285
"I can't wait until the post office starts delivering all these letters to the mayor's office," Julius said. "I

13
00:00:55.286 --> 00:00:59.364
was thinking I could bring some of them to the mayor," Ally said. "Maybe

14
00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:04.397
I can convince her to stop the construction plans when I'm there." "It's

15
00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:11.299
worth a try," Mateo said. "You can be very convincing, Ally." "Sometimes

16
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.526
I'm too convincing," Ally thought. "If

17
00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:24.127
I hadn't helped Sandville grow so quickly, the mayor wouldn't be turning the soccer field into a parking lot." Just

18
00:01:24.128 --> 00:01:27.102
then the doorbell rang. "I'll

19
00:01:27.103 --> 00:01:31.446
get it." Ally answered the door. It

20
00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:33.242
was Barry. "Oh

21
00:01:33.243 --> 00:01:35.192
no!" Ally thought. "I

22
00:01:35.193 --> 00:01:41.601
forgot! I asked him to come over to help me plan Mateo's Holly Days party!" "Hi,

23
00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:45.998
Barry! Did you come to help us write letters?" Ally

24
00:01:45.999 --> 00:01:49.875
gave him a big wink so he'd know to play along. But

25
00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.916
of course Barry didn't get it. "Don't

26
00:01:52.917 --> 00:01:56.277
you remember?" he asked with a frown. "You

27
00:01:56.278 --> 00:01:59.840
asked me to come over so we could talk about something." "Shh!"

28
00:01:59.841 --> 00:02:06.185
Ally whispered. "That's a surprise. Just play along!" "Oh,

29
00:02:06.186 --> 00:02:09.677
right!" Barry said loudly. "I

30
00:02:09.678 --> 00:02:15.285
definitely came here to write letters, lots and lots of letters." "Phew!"

31
00:02:15.286 --> 00:02:23.281
Ally thought. "He finally understood that I was telling a good fib." ***

32
00:02:23.282 --> 00:02:29.173
A few hours later, the kids had a stack of letters and several posters ready to hang up around town.

33
00:02:29.174 --> 00:02:31.844
They'd also prepared the petition.

34
00:02:31.845 --> 00:02:37.409
"Let's meet at the field tomorrow. We'll have the T-shirts then," Mateo said.

35
00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:43.532
"We can also collect signatures on the petition and get more people to write letters," Bethany said. "Great

36
00:02:43.533 --> 00:02:46.341
plan." Julius nodded. Soon

37
00:02:46.342 --> 00:02:51.767
Mateo offered to walk Bethany and Kate home. "And,

38
00:02:51.768 --> 00:02:58.251
uh, I can stay and help you finish cleaning up, Ally," Julius said. "That's

39
00:02:58.252 --> 00:03:02.917
very nice of you," Ally said quickly. "But Barry will help me." "I

40
00:03:02.918 --> 00:03:12.075
will?" Barry asked. Ally winked at him again, and he added, "Oh, yeah, I will!" "Okay,

41
00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:19.298
well, good night then." Julius looked disappointed as he left. Ally

42
00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:25.096
sighed. "I think I just hurt his feelings," she thought. "Too

43
00:03:25.097 --> 00:03:30.638
bad I'm leaving soon. I'd really like to get to know him better." "So,

44
00:03:30.639 --> 00:03:34.505
what do you need help with?" Barry asked. Ally

45
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:40.563
explained her plan to throw a party celebrating all the Holly Days at once for Mateo. "I

46
00:03:40.564 --> 00:03:45.836
want to serve all the traditional foods. It'll be a giant feast!" Barry

47
00:03:45.837 --> 00:03:51.614
laughed. "That sounds like fun. I'll be happy to make the food. This

48
00:03:51.615 --> 00:03:56.372
will be a good chance to show Ray I can do more than wait tables." "Great!

49
00:03:56.373 --> 00:03:59.429
Here's the menu I was thinking of." Ally

50
00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.203
handed Barry a list of dishes she wanted to serve. "Let's

51
00:04:03.204 --> 00:04:06.244
see what you've got." Barry read the list out loud. "'Roasted

52
00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:16.497
turkey with chocolate sauce, ham with candy eggs, potato pancakes with gravy, and sweet potatoes with rice cakes.' This

53
00:04:16.498 --> 00:04:25.191
menu is, er, interesting. But I'll do whatever you ask!" ***

54
00:04:25.192 --> 00:04:31.439
After Barry left, Ally went into her room and booted up Alpha. "Hi,

55
00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.080
Alpha! Let's play some quiet music." "Why

56
00:04:36.081 --> 00:04:39.420
don't you ask your other phone," Alpha said. "There

57
00:04:39.421 --> 00:04:43.008
is no other phone!" Ally said. "Then

58
00:04:43.009 --> 00:04:48.008
what is this device next to me?" Alpha asked. "Well,

59
00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:53.609
it's another phone, but I only have it because Kate gave it to me." "Illogical.

60
00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.359
You have another phone." "But

61
00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:03.369
I only have it because I told Kate that I'd lost you. It was a harmless fib." "

62
00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:07.846
Harmless and fib are incompatible words," Alpha snapped.

63
00:05:07.847 --> 00:05:15.732
"Not always," Ally said. "Mateo said it's okay to fib on Earth as long as no one gets hurt."

64
00:05:15.733 --> 00:05:19.257
"Harumph! I guess you consider me no one then!"

65
00:05:19.258 --> 00:05:27.898
Alpha's screen went black as she turned herself off.

